Justice Crispin addressed Anu directly saying, in the next few years you will have come to terms with the fact that you killed the man you loved. You have caused immense pain. If you find the moral courage you may be able to rebuild from this wreckage to repay the trust people have put in you. He then declared her not guilty of Joe Chinquay's murder but guilty to manslaughter on the grounds of diminished responsibility. Anu Singh was sentenced to 10 years in prison with a non-parole period of four years backdated to the time of Joe's death. This meant she would be eligible for release in a little over two years. The short sentence devastated the Chinquay family. When Justice Crispin left the

