00:53:12.000 --> 00:54:08.000
family suffered. I don't put any blame on Mardavi. Anu served her sentence at the Silverwater Correctional Complex, a maximum security prison 20 kilometers west of the Sydney CBD, where she worked in the prison library and tutored other inmates. She underwent psychotherapy and was prescribed with medication used to treat a range of mental health issues, including depression, anxiety and obsessive compulsive disorder. She was eventually transferred to the Emu Claims Correctional Center and granted day release to attend classes at the University of Sydney, where she obtained a master's in criminology. In October of 2001, she was released on parole at the age of 29. In 2004, she breached her parole

